WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.168
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03.218 --> 00:00:07.031
AI for Young Builders, video 2.

3
00:00:07.081 --> 00:00:09.275
Rules or learning?

4
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:11.020
How AI learns.

5
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.122
There are two ways to make a computer smart.

6
00:00:16.172 --> 00:00:17.584
One is very old.

7
00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:21.880
The other powers almost every AI you use today.

8
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.973
The old way is rules.

9
00:00:25.023 --> 00:00:31.392
A person writes exact instructions, like: if the temperature is above thirty

10
00:00:31.442 --> 00:00:33.672
degrees, switch on the fan.

11
00:00:33.722 --> 00:00:39.330
The program takes an input, follows the rules, and gives an answer.

12
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.891
Now try writing rules for: is this a photo of a cat?

13
00:00:44.941 --> 00:00:50.256
Cats can be big or small, orange or striped, sleeping, jumping or

14
00:00:50.306 --> 00:00:52.236
hiding behind a curtain.

15
00:00:52.286 --> 00:00:55.620
You would never finish writing the rules.

16
00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.739
So machine learning flips it around.

17
00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:05.810
You give the computer lots of examples, and the right answers, called labels.

18
00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.595
It finds the patterns itself and builds a model.

19
00:01:09.645 --> 00:01:14.720
Then you give the model something new, and it makes a prediction.

20
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:20.476
Machine learning always follows five steps.

21
00:01:20.526 --> 00:01:22.246
Collect examples.

22
00:01:22.296 --> 00:01:23.391
Label them.

23
00:01:23.441 --> 00:01:24.849
Train a model.

24
00:01:24.899 --> 00:01:28.805
Test it on examples it has never seen.

25
00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.470
And then use it.

26
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:36.300
If the test goes badly, go back and collect better data.

27
00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.607
So which should you use?

28
00:01:39.657 --> 00:01:44.793
Ringing the school bell at nine o’clock needs one simple rule.

29
00:01:44.843 --> 00:01:50.731
But reading handwriting, or spotting spam, is messy and keeps changing.

30
00:01:50.781 --> 00:01:53.240
That is where learning shines.

31
00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.963
Let us recap.

32
00:01:56.013 --> 00:02:00.406
Normal programs follow rules a person wrote.

33
00:02:00.456 --> 00:02:06.062
Machine learning finds the rules from labelled examples.

34
00:02:06.112 --> 00:02:10.808
The steps are collect, label, train, test, use.

35
00:02:10.858 --> 00:02:14.040
Next: Data: features and labels.
